{"ID": 1462474511122436366, "Timestamp": "2026-01-18 15:51:34", "Contents": "Salamualaykum.\n\n<@1405550223610220587> you can unreserve. I went ahead and reserved Manara Al Muna (Mecca) with our new dates and sent a request to adjust the dates at Taibah Apartments (Medina).\n\nManara Al Muna (Mecca) - Mon check in to Friday check out (4 nights)\nTaibah (Medina) - Friday check in to Sunday check out (2 nights)", "Attachments": ""},
{"ID": 1461542825236762634, "Timestamp": "2026-01-16 02:09:23", "Contents": "And if you want to do it more than once, it makes more sense to have more time in Mecca", "Attachments": ""},
{"ID": 1461542753652703366, "Timestamp": "2026-01-16 02:09:06", "Contents": "Medina doesn’t have anything to do with ummrah", "Attachments": ""},
{"ID": 1461532530510528592, "Timestamp": "2026-01-16 01:28:29", "Contents": "4 nights Mecca then 2 nights Medina with some of the last day in Medina before taking a train to Jeddah.", "Attachments": ""},
{"ID": 1461529106452578425, "Timestamp": "2026-01-16 01:14:52", "Contents": "I think we should transfer one of our Medina day to Mecca", "Attachments": ""},
{"ID": 1461529027046019123, "Timestamp": "2026-01-16 01:14:33", "Contents": "We need time to visit even one of these places. We can fully expect Hira to be packed. The others likely will be too.", "Attachments": ""},
{"ID": 1461528780370739331, "Timestamp": "2026-01-16 01:13:35", "Contents": "For example, Meccan Ziyarat. Ziyarat is a pilgrimage to places associated with the Prophet peace be upon him. These places exist obviously in both cities, so you can make ziyarat in both. The Cave of Hira is one of these places and it’s in Mecca. Jannat Al Mualla, the cemetery where Khadijah, may Allah be pleased with her, is also in Mecca. In fairness, there are plenty of ziyarat sites in Medina. Many mosques that the Prophet (pbuh) prayed in or prepared in for battle or after battle. Uhud mountain is there.", "Attachments": ""},
{"ID": 1461526566650642537, "Timestamp": "2026-01-16 01:04:47", "Contents": "Doing it once in one trip is good enough for me. Like Brandon said, it’s a big thing and we should appreciate the experience fully. Besides,  there’s more to do in Mecca, and after speaking to my mother, I think itd be better to spend more time in Mecca.", "Attachments": ""},
{"ID": 1461494681966874881, "Timestamp": "2026-01-15 22:58:05", "Contents": "I'm going to do some more research on our options. You guys should as well", "Attachments": ""},
{"ID": 1461494598126800926, "Timestamp": "2026-01-15 22:57:45", "Contents": "Fair point.", "Attachments": ""},
{"ID": 1461494387044516092, "Timestamp": "2026-01-15 22:56:55", "Contents": "Pull up the $9k/night one, Mohammed", "Attachments": ""},
{"ID": 1461494274800619551, "Timestamp": "2026-01-15 22:56:28", "Contents": "What if we splurged on a nice hotel for the second Mecca stay? To end the trip.", "Attachments": ""},
{"ID": 1461493924987408620, "Timestamp": "2026-01-15 22:55:04", "Contents": "From what we've reserved, Mecca is cheaper yes.", "Attachments": ""},
{"ID": 1461493137125146687, "Timestamp": "2026-01-15 22:51:57", "Contents": "At least back when she did umrah, but I'm not sure for the present.", "Attachments": ""},
{"ID": 1461493001351331851, "Timestamp": "2026-01-15 22:51:24", "Contents": "Also, my grandmother told me that the base of clock tower next to Al Haram distributes breakfast for free during ramadan, and there are cafes/restaurants around there as well that are paid.", "Attachments": ""},
{"ID": 1461492698933624955, "Timestamp": "2026-01-15 22:50:12", "Contents": "I will, inshaAllah", "Attachments": ""},
{"ID": 1461492418653192342, "Timestamp": "2026-01-15 22:49:05", "Contents": "My mom said it would be better for us to enjoy Mecca for more time than Medina. She suggests we make our Medina stay in the middle of the week for a day or two. So we could start in Mecca (Mon-Wed), then go to Medina (Wed-Fri), then back to Mecca until departure (Fri-Sun).", "Attachments": ""},
{"ID": 1461485024669859972, "Timestamp": "2026-01-15 22:19:42", "Contents": "Mecca hotel to Al Haram ~ 2 hours\nMedina hotel to Al Nabawi ~ 40 minutes", "Attachments": ""},
